From: Weikai Kong <priv@pppig236.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jan 2025 16:02:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sm8450-common: Use rear ALS for brightness

Seems to be better than the wise light since it is not under screen

Change-Id: I57393ec362e002139594fe7f395b0d9d9df41dab
Signed-off-by: Weikai Kong <priv@pppig236.com>
---
 overlay/OPlusFrameworksResCommon/res/values/config.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/overlay/OPlusFrameworksResCommon/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/OPlusFrameworksResCommon/res/values/config.xml
index 3ef78e0..f6858e2 100644
--- a/overlay/OPlusFrameworksResCommon/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/OPlusFrameworksResCommon/res/values/config.xml
@@ -120,5 +120,5 @@
 
     <!-- The type of the light sensor to be used by the display framework for things like
          auto-brightness. If unset, then it just gets the default sensor of type TYPE_LIGHT. -->
-    <string name="config_displayLightSensorType" translatable="false">qti.sensor.wise_light</string>
+    <string name="config_displayLightSensorType" translatable="false">qti.sensor.light_rear</string>
 </resources>
